For developers building applications, using a JavaScript library gives you full control. The most popular option is marked:

```bash
npm install marked
```

```javascript
import { marked } from 'marked';

const markdown = '# Hello World\n\nThis is **bold** text.';
const html = marked.parse(markdown);

console.log(html);
// <h1>Hello World</h1>
// <p>This is <strong>bold</strong> text.</p>
```

Key benefits:
- Runs in browser or Node.js
- Customizable renderers
- Supports GitHub Flavored Markdown
- Active community with regular updates

Use this when you need to convert Markdown programmatically in your own applications.
